#. §5: `Q ∧ (R ∧ S)`
#. §6: `(Q ∧ R) ∧ S`
#. §7: `S ∧ (Q ∧ R)`
#. §8: ```
#. rw[And_comm (Q ∧ R)]
#. ```
#. §9: ```
#. rw[And_comm (Q ∧ R) S]
#. ```
#. §10: ```
#. rw[And_comm _ S]
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L04_equiv
msgid "**Here's what happened:** Lean searched for the **first instance** of\n"
"§0\n"
"where the underscores are wildcards. The first underscore was matched with §1, the second with §2. Lean then applied §3 (from *right-to-left*) to this instance. In particular, Lean substituted §4 for §5.\n"
"\n"
"Now we'd like to **commute** the expression §6 to get §7. 👉 We can accomplish this with either:\n"
"§8\n"
"or\n"
"§9\n"
"or even\n"
"§10\n"
"This last form is slightly dangerous in this case though; 🤔 can you tell why?"
msgstr ""

